-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: who is insured under Chapters 5, 6, 7 (s 158), 8, 9, 10 and 11 (and s 6B). Row IL-33.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew before the run; the working is beside each group.
-- Unless a day is given the day is 15 January 2026.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Wrappers`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 5 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 75 — insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 6 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 150 — insured under Chapter 6:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 7 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 158 and s 6B — insured under Chapter 7:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 158(1) for` p `on` d MEANS `s 158 — insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 8 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 180-181 — a worker insured under Chapter 8:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 9 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 195 — insured under Chapter 9:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 10 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 223 — insured for long-term care:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 11 for` p `on` d MEANS `s 240 — insured under Chapter 11:` p `on` d `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Fixtures — persons`

-- Avi: a man born 10 March 1988, an employee in Israel, resident since birth.
avi MEANS `an Israeli employee` "Avi" `born` (YMD 1988 3 10) `who is` `male`
-- Batya: a woman born 20 June 1990, not working, resident since birth.
batya MEANS `a person` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1990 6 20)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`

§ `Tests — the two ordinary persons (day 15 January 2026)`

-- Avi, 37 years 10 months: a resident (lives in Israel, no s 2A permission), 18 or over, a man whose
-- retirement age and Part B age are 804 months (Part A and B, "May 1942 and after: 67"), whose age is 454
-- months; an employee in Israel (s 75(a)(1)); entitled to wages; not a controlling shareholder; on first
-- becoming a resident (his birth) 0 months old, below Part C's 744. Insured in every Chapter.
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `section 158(1) for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 7 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 8 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 9 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 10 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 11 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

-- Batya, 35 years: not an employee, not self-employed, in no further category: not insured under Chapter 5,
-- Chapter 7 or Chapter 8 (she neither is nor was an employee). She is insured under Chapters 6, 9, 10 and 11:
-- a resident of 18 or over who has not reached the retirement age (s 3 of the Retirement Age Law: 65 years for a
-- woman born after 1969, 780 months, reached 20 June 2055); on first becoming a resident (her birth) she was
-- 0 months old.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `section 158(1) for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 7 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 8 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 9 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 10 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 11 for` batya `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§ `Tests — Chapter 5 (ss 75-76)`

§§ `(1) an employee; the three left out; (2) the self-employed; (3) to (8) the further categories`

-- A police officer, prison officer or security-service employee is left out of (1) and is in no other
-- category here.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Cop" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee in Israel, controlling` FALSE `, kibbutz member` FALSE `, entitled to wages` TRUE `, police type` TRUE `, insured earlier` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- The self-employed in Israel: (2). Of an excluded class: not.
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Sam" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` `the work of a self-employed person in Israel`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Sam" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a self-employed person, abroad` FALSE `, of an excluded class` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A self-employed person working outside Israel: s 75(a)(2) says nothing about place (fork C3). By default
-- declined; "insured wherever the work is done": insured; "only if in Israel": not.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Sam" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a self-employed person, abroad` TRUE `, of an excluded class` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `s 75 — insured under Chapter 5:` (`a person` "Sam" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a self-employed person, abroad` TRUE `, of an excluded class` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a self-employed person who works outside Israel` `read as` `insured wherever the work is done`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 75 — insured under Chapter 5:` (`a person` "Sam" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a self-employed person, abroad` TRUE `, of an excluded class` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a self-employed person who works outside Israel` `read as` `insured only if the work is done in Israel`)
-- Abroad and of an excluded class: not insured whatever the reading (the chain stops at the first FALSE).
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Sam" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a self-employed person, abroad` TRUE `, of an excluded class` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- Each further category (3) to (8): a person who does not work and is in it is insured.
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Ron" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a person in the further category` `in vocational training or rehabilitation at a place or with a person approved in regulations, section 75(a)(3)`)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Ron" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of a person in the further category` `a person whose wage is fixed by law, section 75(a)(8)`)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A person who is in no category is not insured.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Nobody" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A visitor (not a resident) who is an employee in Israel is insured: s 75(a)(1) names no residence.
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§§ `s 76: an employee who works abroad`

-- (a): insured if employee and employer are residents and the contract was made in Israel, "or even if" it was
-- not made in Israel and there is no compulsory work-injury insurance at the workplace and notice was given.
-- (b): after more than five consecutive years abroad, not insured unless permitted.
-- Columns: employer resident, contract made in Israel, no compulsory insurance, notice given, over five
-- years, permitted.
-- T1 TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE: contract in Israel -> insured.
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` TRUE `, no compulsory insurance` FALSE `, notice given` FALSE `, over five years` FALSE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- T2 TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE: contract elsewhere, no compulsory insurance, notice given -> insured.
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` FALSE `, no compulsory insurance` TRUE `, notice given` TRUE `, over five years` FALSE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- T3 compulsory insurance applies at the workplace -> not.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` FALSE `, no compulsory insurance` FALSE `, notice given` TRUE `, over five years` FALSE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- T4 no notice -> not.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` FALSE `, no compulsory insurance` TRUE `, notice given` FALSE `, over five years` FALSE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- T5 the employer is not a resident -> not (the residence of both stays in both branches).
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` FALSE `, contract made in Israel` TRUE `, no compulsory insurance` TRUE `, notice given` TRUE `, over five years` FALSE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- T6 more than five consecutive years: not, unless permitted.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` TRUE `, no compulsory insurance` FALSE `, notice given` FALSE `, over five years` TRUE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1980 1 1)) `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` TRUE `, no compulsory insurance` FALSE `, notice given` FALSE `, over five years` TRUE `, permitted` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- T7 the employee does not live in Israel (not a resident): not.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 5 for` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1980 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` `a person living abroad` `and` (`the work of an employee abroad, employer resident` TRUE `, contract made in Israel` TRUE `, no compulsory insurance` FALSE `, notice given` FALSE `, over five years` FALSE `, permitted` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§ `Tests — Chapters 6 and 9 (ss 150, 195): 18 and the retirement age`

-- A man born 1 March 1959: 804 months after is 1 March 2026. Insured on 28 February 2026, not on 1 March 2026.
