§ `Tests — Chapter 10, long-term care (s 223)`

-- (1) anyone insured under Chapter 11; (4) a resident who immigrated under the Law of Return, or holds a
-- permanent-residence or A/5 visa and licence, and was given an absorption basket, if not insured under
-- Chapter 11.
#ASSERT `Chapter 10 for` avi `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 10 for` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` TRUE `, visa holder` FALSE `, basket` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Chapter 10 for` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` FALSE `, visa holder` TRUE `, basket` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- s 223 (4): an immigrant under the Law of Return, resident, not insured under Chapter 11, with no absorption basket. Does the basket
-- qualify the immigrant too (fork L1)? If it qualifies both limbs he is not insured; if only the visa holder he is; the default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Chapter 10 for` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` TRUE `, visa holder` FALSE `, basket` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 223 — insured for long-term care:` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` TRUE `, visa holder` FALSE `, basket` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the absorption basket in section 223 "insured" (4)` `read as` `the absorption basket qualifies both the immigrant and the visa holder`)
#ASSERT `s 223 — insured for long-term care:` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` TRUE `, visa holder` FALSE `, basket` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the absorption basket in section 223 "insured" (4)` `read as` `the absorption basket qualifies only the visa holder`)
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 10 for` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` FALSE `, visa holder` FALSE `, basket` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

-- A visa holder without a basket, and a person with neither immigration nor visa but a basket: not insured on either reading
-- (the two limbs agree), so the default answers.
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 10 for` ((`a person` "Olim" `born` (YMD 1950 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with the absorption facts` (`absorption facts: immigrant` FALSE `, visa holder` TRUE `, basket` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

-- s 158(3): the case says a woman served at least six months and married within 30 days, but gives 5 months served: the facts
-- contradict each other and the answer is declined by name (not trusted from the flag).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 158 — insured under paragraph (3), a completed national or community service:` (batya `with the completed service` (`a service of` 5 `months ended` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, civil-national:` FALSE `, began before 31 August 2026:` TRUE `, woman married within 30 days:` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
